        <p>As further proof of the fact that Veno's Lightning Cough Cure is the cure that always cures, Mrs. Dainty,- of 31, Spout-lane, Walsall, sends the following account of her little boy's Cure from a Chronic Cough, Whooping Cough, and Blood Spitting. "My boy, Leslie, 8 years old, had been troubled from birth with a nasty cough which two months ago developed into Whooping Cough, and then started spitting blood. Doctor's medicine did him no good, co in despair I gave him Veno's Lightning Cough Cure, and judge our delight when after only two doses the Blood-spitting was greatly lessened, and in about a week the cough was quite gone, and the Blood-spitting stopped altogether. I can honestly say that since taking Veto's Lightning Cough Cure he has never been I troubled with a cough of any sort." The Pro- prietors of Veno's Lightning Cough Cure are daily receiving letters similar to Mrs. Dainty's, which is pleasing testimony to the enormous popularity and efficacy of their now standard remedy. Veno's Lightning Cough Cure can be obtained for 914., mid, and 2/9 of all chemists.</p>
        <p>The St. Asaph Rural District Council on Sat- urday declined to agree to the proposed basis of contribution to the suggested new highway between RhYl and Gronant, as, it was stated, the new roadway would benefit the district but slightly.</p>
        <p>The vicariate of Barrowford, near Nelson._ vacant by the resignation of the Rev. A. E. Studdy-Studdy, has been filled by the appoint- ment of the Rev. F. W. Fairhurst, curate-in- charge of Carrington, just over the border of Cheshire.</p>
