      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-12-27_WidnesExaminer_art0177" n="art0177">
        <head>AMIDST THE PLEASURES.</head>
        <p>AMIDST THE PLEASURES.</p>
        <p>My dear Children,— I know you are now revelling amidst</p>
        <p>the pleasures and joys of the Chrislimastide, and looking forward to more fun at the New Year, so I shall not bother you with a long letter. I must, however, wish you all a very, very happy New Year, and I hope that ere the year 1914 is very old we shall have got over 100 new members. We are getting well on for that figure now. _ _</p>
        <p>I am pleased to think our Corner is so appre- iated, and I was delighted to receive the follow- ng later from a new niece :</p>
        <p>"Dear Uncle Jack,-1 have been reading The Examiner' each week, and I noticed that a great many children have joined your Corner. I was reading last week about the 'Lost Pearl of Queen Rosamond,' and I enjoyed the story very much. I should be very pleased, indeed, if you. would, enrol me as one of your mem- bers.</p>
        <p>" NELLIE MASON.</p>
        <p>" 174, Longford-street, Warrington." We are delighted to welcome our new cousin, Ind hope she will get some of her friends to join.</p>
        <p>Your loving UNCLE JACK.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-12-27_WidnesExaminer_art0178" n="art0178">
        <head>GREAT EXPECTAT</head>
        <p>GREAT EXPECTAT</p>
        <p>ONS.</p>
        <p>Little Tommy I reckon Santa Clam can't get much into my stocking, so I guess I'll just hang up this 'ere bag instead."</p>
        <p>CONUNDRUMS.</p>
        <p>Why is a bee-hive like a spectator?—Because L is a bee-holder.</p>
        <p>Why is a jest like a chicken?—Because there is a. merry-thought in it. Why is a man walking to a town like one about to prevent a blow?—Because he is going to-Ward it.</p>
