        <p>as possible victors. The teams will probably he:</p>
        <p>while at the opposite end Redford followed suit. From a free kick the visitors gained no advan- tage, the ball going dead. This brought relief to the hoine defence, and, the visitors' goal !ad a wrow escape. Bad shooting spoiled chances to both teams. Even play followed, but no score was recorded, and at half-time the score-sheet Waz blank, On restarting both teams played vigorously, was visited, the Juniors having and each e_ .'4 19110 t erratically. The visit- most chances, bu. -4 from a miskiok by one 4 r ors now,had a turn, an.. --4iworth uhed iP of the home defenders Shut,_ ~..062,80 op and opened the score. From this _ -.1311§1 home team played excitedly. The Barn.. attacked strongly, but were held at bay by some good play by the home backs. The Juniors again missed several chances of equalising owing to their forwards' bad shooting, and the Barnabas' forwards, by good combination, trans- ferred play to the home area, when Woods scored a second goal. The play became very keen and players on both sides reverted to shady tactics. Towards the close the Juniors had the hest of play, but failed to take the chances that were presented to them, and the whistle blew with the result: St. Barnabas', two goals; Caford Juniors, none.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON. Jolley.</p>
        <p>Bradshaw, Dickensoß; Tranter, Ruddick. Nicholas, Yoiing.</p>
        <p>Chesters, Cox, SkelhOrne, . Thomas, Clare,</p>
        <p>Wigan Bottled' Up and Defeated hy the Wilderspooi</p>
        <p>Fearnley. E. Thomas.</p>
        <p>men's Bustling Tactics.</p>
        <p>Riehie, Rees, Thom,_ *van, .Goldsmith,</p>
        <p>May, John,</p>
        <p>Callender, W. Thomas, Loveluck, Mesley</p>
        <p>Launce. SALFORD.</p>
        <p>ntary Day- the )f the 1 was</p>
        <p>On New Year's Day Warrington go to Run- corn, and special trains will be run. The second team meet at Wilderspool. At eleven o'clock on New Year's morning the Lancashire Junior Cup final will be decided on the Wilders- pool pitch between Rylands' and Abram Rangers. All members will have to pay for this match. Huddersfield are due at Wilders- pool on Saturday, 3rd January.</p>
